odrigues hit Erik Gustafsson","type":{"id":"503","text":"Hit","abbreviation":"hit"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:45"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"11"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3648008","displayName":"Evan Rodrigues","shortName":"E. Rodrigues"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"3891922","displayName":"Erik Gustafsson","shortName":"E. Gustafsson"},"type":"hitted"}]},{"id":"401892567000001070","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Giveaway by Anthony Mantha","type":{"id":"1402","text":"Giveaway","abbreviation":"giveaway"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:56"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"11"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3042037","displayName":"Anthony Mantha","shortName":"A. Mantha"},"type":"giver"}]},{"id":"401892567000000970","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Brett Pesce Hooking against Alex Laferriere","type":{"id":"33","text":"Hooking","abbreviation":"Hooking"},"clock":{"displayValue":"3:09"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"11"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3025535","displayName":"Brett Pesce","shortName":"B. Pesce"}},{"athlete":{"id":"4697725","displayName":"Alex Laferriere","shortName":"A. Laferriere"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1826","fullName":"Prudential Center","address":{"city":"Newark","state":"NJ","zipCode":"07199","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1826.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":16019,"officials":[{"fullName":"TJ Luxmore","displayName":"TJ Luxmore","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Libor Suchanek","displayName":"Libor Suchanek","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jesse Marquis","displayName":"Jesse Marquis","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Corey Syvret","displayName":"Corey Syvret","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Brett Pesce scores go-ahead goal as Devils beat Kings 3-1 for 3rd straight win","description":"— Brett Pesce scored the go-ahead goal and Jake Allen made 12 saves as the New Jersey Devils beat the Los Angeles Kings 3-1 on Saturday for their third straight win.","story":"NEWARK, N.J. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3025535/brett-pesce\">Brett Pesce</a> scored the go-ahead goal and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5111/jake-allen\">Jake Allen</a> made 12 saves as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/la/los-angeles-kings\">Los Angeles Kings</a> 3-1 on Saturday for their third straight win.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042037/anthony-mantha\">Anthony Mantha</a> and Artemy Gritsyuk also scored for the Devils, who also beat Colorado and Anaheim on their current homestand. New Jersey has won five of six. Allen improved to 5-2-0 this season.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976848/scott-laughton\">Scott Laughton</a> scored for Los Angeles, which saw its two-game winning streak snapped. Forsberg made 23 saves.\n\n\r\n              Pesce beat goaltender <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3036851/anton-forsberg\">Anton Forsberg</a> at 8:08 of the third period after the defenseman found a clear lane through traffic in the Los Angeles zone. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697446/luke-evangelista\">Luke Evangelista</a> and Gritsyuk assisted on Pesce’s first goal this season.\n\n\r\n              Before the game, the Devils introduced newly acquired goaltender <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/connor-hellebuyck-new-jersey-devils-96dc6e927584899f6bb654ba0d58154a\"><a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3020225/connor-hellebuyck\">Connor Hellebuyck</a></a>. The 33-year-old Hellebuyck won 345 games in 11 seasons with Winnipeg and is a three-time winner of the Vezina Trophy.\n\n\r\n              New Jersey included goaltender <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697683/nico-daws\">Nico Daws</a>, who won against Anaheim on Thursday, in <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/hellebuyck-trade-devils-jets-26c70cac1b23930670e1200f298ac80e\">the trade for Hellebuyck</a> on Friday. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697829/remi-poirier\">Remi Poirier</a>, who has yet to play an NHL game, dressed as Allen’s backup on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Laughton scored at 15:57 of the second, driving the puck past Allen for his second goal. \n\n\r\n              Mantha tied the game about three minutes later with his third goal.\n\n\r\n              Gritsyuk scored his team-leading sixth goal into an empty net at 18:55. \n\n\r\n              The Kings had a power-play chance when New Jersey's <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899978/timo-meier\">Timo Meier</a> was called for tripping at 12:59 of the third but were unable to tie the game.\n\n\r\n              Los Angeles was coming off road wins over Washington and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyi/new-york-islanders\">New York Islanders</a> to start its five-game trip after losing its first six games.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Kings: At the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a> on Monday.\n\n\r\n              Devils: At Dallas on Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-24T22:13:46Z"}}